    "map":  {
                "$comment":  "Empty on purpose. What each Alpha control does is Mark\u0027s decision (see notes/alpha-plan.md), taken after the physical map is measured. Same shape as the Bravo\u0027s map: press / release / when, controls as FSUIPC numbers or preset names."
            },
    "numbering":  "prober = the number the Windows Game Controllers panel shows (1-based). fsuipc = prober - 1, and 100 more when that is above 31 (FSUIPC7 User Guide; checked on a Bravo: panel 33 = FSUIPC 132). A hat is not a button: its entries carry hat (the direction) and fsuipc from the FSUIPC7 User Guide rule, POV = buttons 32 (forward) to 39 clockwise, marked assumed until a FSUIPC7.log line has shown it.",
    "coverage":  "All 35 buttons Windows reports are accounted for (2026-09-07): 1-12 the yoke (trigger, two white, red, eight rocker positions), 13-30 the nine base switches (odd ON, next even OFF, in otherPosition), 31-35 the key (OFF, R, L, BOTH, START). The hat is a separate switch, not a button. Two axes (aileron, elevator) are not in this table."
